    "title": "Tell City police officer rescues injured owl - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Ian Young ,\n1 hours ago\nHENDERSON, Ky. (WEHT) — A Tell City police officer was off on an unusual assignment.\nAccording to the Tell City Police Department, Officer Clay James discovered an owl with a wing injury while patrolling. Officials say the owl was injured following a vehicle collision.\nOfficers say James rescued the owl, made sure it was in stable condition and turned it over to The Talon Trust organization for recovery and rehabilitation.\n“We are proud of Officer James for showing compassion and professionalism in protecting all members of our community, even the feathered ones,” says the Tell City Police Department.\nEyewitness News. Everywhere you are.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to Eyewitness News (WEHT/WTVW).",
    "summary": "HENDERSON, Ky. (WEHT) — A Tell City police officer was off on an unusual assignment. According to the Tell City Police Department, Officer Clay James discovered an owl with a wing injury while patrolling. Officers say James rescued the owl, made sure it was in stable condition and turned it over to The Talon Trust organization for recovery and rehabilitation. “We are proud of Officer James for showing compassion and professionalism in protecting all members of our community, even the feathered ones,” says the Tell City Police Department. Copyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved.",
